<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Algorithm of Self-Critique</h2>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Self-Critique Contamination Detection</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
          Model <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> (black-box with per-token log-prob access or top-<math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> probs), meta-prompt <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\text{critique}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mtext>critique</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\text{critique}}</annotation></semantics></math>, problem <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
          Contamination score <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Score}(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Score</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Score}(q)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Deterministic decoding.</span> Use greedy decoding (temperature <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=0</annotation></semantics></math>) in all generations.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
          
</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Initial response)</span> Construct <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}\leftarrow T(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}\leftarrow T(q)</annotation></semantics></math> and generate <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}\leftarrow\mathcal{M}(P_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}\leftarrow\mathcal{M}(P_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
          Compute token-level entropy sequence <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{1}\leftarrow\{H_{t}(r_{1})\}_{t=1}^{|r_{1}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{1}\leftarrow\{H_{t}(r_{1})\}_{t=1}^{|r_{1}|}</annotation></semantics></math> using per-token probabilities.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Self-critique response)</span> Form <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime}\leftarrow q\oplus I_{\text{critique}}(r_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mtext>critique</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime}\leftarrow q\oplus I_{\text{critique}}(r_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>; construct <math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{2}\leftarrow T(q^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{2}\leftarrow T(q^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> and generate <math id="alg1.l7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{2}\leftarrow\mathcal{M}(P_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{2}\leftarrow\mathcal{M}(P_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
          Compute entropy sequence <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{2}\leftarrow\{H_{t}(r_{2})\}_{t=1}^{|r_{2}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{2}\leftarrow\{H_{t}(r_{2})\}_{t=1}^{|r_{2}|}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Similarity)</span> Pad the shorter sequence with zeros:
<math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{E}_{1}\leftarrow\text{pad}(E_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>pad</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{E}_{1}\leftarrow\text{pad}(E_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>,  <math id="alg1.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{E}_{2}\leftarrow\text{pad}(E_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>pad</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{E}_{2}\leftarrow\text{pad}(E_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
          Compute cosine similarity <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leftarrow\cos(\tilde{E}_{1},\tilde{E}_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leftarrow\cos(\tilde{E}_{1},\tilde{E}_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
          Compute length penalty <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\leftarrow\frac{\min(|E_{1}|,|E_{2}|)}{\max(|E_{1}|,|E_{2}|)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\leftarrow\frac{\min(|E_{1}|,|E_{2}|)}{\max(|E_{1}|,|E_{2}|)}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Score}(q)\leftarrow s\times\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Score</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Score}(q)\leftarrow s\times\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Additional Results</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Additional Results on Qwen2.5-7B-Math</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Table <a href="#A2.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ B.1 Additional Results on Qwen2.5-7B-Math ‣ Appendix B Additional Results ‣ Detecting Data Contamination from Reinforcement Learning Post-training for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, on Qwen2.5-7B-Math, Self-Critique achieves the best AUC on both AIME24 (0.76) and AIME25 (0.72), and the highest average AUC (0.74). The two entropy baselines are competitive, while likelihood-based methods (PPL, Min-K%, Min-K%++) and Recall/CDD are clearly weaker here. We do not report K&amp;K and SAT for this model because we could not get stable RL training on these synthetic datasets with a non-instruct base; such setups typically require more careful RL hyperparameters and data curation. This engineering detail is outside the scope of our study.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Detection results on <span id="A2.T5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qwen2.5-7B-Math</span> under RL-MIA (higher is better).
AVG reports mean AUC across AIME24 and AIME25.</figcaption>
<div id="A2.T5.4" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:318.0pt;height:82.4pt;vertical-align:-39.5pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-76.3pt,19.8pt) scale(0.675659447308864,0.675659447308864) ;">
